    Fix Brightspace UDP deserialization failure for API change and handle unknown JSON properties (#7507)
    
    Brightspace's UserData API returns a `FirstLoginDate` property not present in `BrightspaceUser`, causing Jackson deserialization to fail and breaking the Brightspace user directory provider.
    
    ## Changes
    
    - **`BrightspaceUser.java`**
    - Add `@JsonIgnoreProperties(ignoreUnknown = true)` to tolerate
    future/unknown Brightspace API fields without failing deserialization
    - Add `firstLoginDate` field mapped to `@JsonProperty("FirstLoginDate")`
    with constructor parameter and `getFirstLoginDate()` accessor
    
    ```java
    @JsonIgnoreProperties(ignoreUnknown = true)
    public class BrightspaceUser {
      // ...
      private String firstLoginDate;
    
      @JsonCreator
      public BrightspaceUser(
          // ...
          @JsonProperty("FirstLoginDate") String firstLoginDate
      ) {
        // ...
        this.firstLoginDate = firstLoginDate;
      }
    
      public String getFirstLoginDate() {
        return this.firstLoginDate;
      }
    }
    ```
    
    Backport of
    [cilt-uct/opencast@d7ae5b7](https://github.com/cilt-uct/opencast/commit/d7ae5b77876054f9642e67f62aa1d8bd9f24acbd)
    onto `r/19.x`.
    
